    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1684">

                <pb facs="1375" n="1259" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1259"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 419.11 D 29/31.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Chargé d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 88.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 12, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 238,
                    of the 28th ultimo, in which you report that you have addressed a note to the
                    Panaman Foreign Office calling attention to the necessity of apprehending those
                    members of the national police force, who were guilty of the unjustifiable
                    assault upon American citizens on July 4 last, as being an in <pb facs="1376"
                        n="1260" xml:id="pg1260"/> dispensable part of any adjustment of the case
                    between the two Governments.</p>
                <p>Your action in the matter is approved.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
